  "reason": "The typescript-output-v1 freeze left the lockfile, the vendored npm cache tree hash, the formatter hash and the reference verification to amendment 001 (CONTRACT.md section 7). After the one approved npm download (2026-10-21) every pinned version was fetched, no package needs an install script, and no network access followed. This amendment seals reference/package-lock.json and the toolchain.json values, records a hand-written example-v1 reference product that passes install, typecheck, format_check and test offline with the lockfile unchanged, and adds npm_config_logs_dir and npm_config_userconfig to the command environment so npm writes nothing into the read-only cache, and toolchain.json postgresql.start notes that pg_ctl start runs with LC_ALL=C on this host (an operational finding of the run). The reference run also showed that prettier's default quoteProps prints identifier keys without quotes, so the naming wording in product-layout.json, scope.json and CONTRACT.md now asks for bracket reads and own-property checks instead of quoted keys; the refused names and the generated semantics are unchanged.",
